Option: winter-hide-tomatoes
Name: Hide the tomatoes and basil while the page is in its winter look
Does: When the season on screen is winter (the page opens on winter from Nov 9, and the Christmas tree weekends), the home page leaves out the rest of what offers u-pick tomatoes and basil: the Things to Do menu line, the whole Tomatoes & basil section with its varieties (one CSS line), the add-on, the calendar row, the FAQ entry and the FAQ list line, the email sign-up interest, and the farm map's tomato field and its legend line. The all-year first-screen line, the "Season by season" Fall cell and the Fall tab name say the same thing without the tomatoes. (The Store tomato card and its button and the Pumpkin patch page card are already hidden in winter with the Store farm group and that page.) In spring, summer and fall nothing changes (the changes are attributes, one CSS line that only matches winter, and three winter-only lines that stay hidden). The tour skips its two tomato cards when their parts are not on the page. The pizza words (tomato sauce, tomatoes on a pizza) and the Fall tab and card of "What's on the farm" stay as they are.
Answers: d93 A (tomatoes and basil in winter)
Conflicts: none
Requires: none
Host: any
Order: 15
After: python3 tools/pages.py, then python3 tools/i18n.py extract, then python3 tools/i18n.py jsstrings, then python3 tools/i18n.py build, then python3 tools/i18n.py missing es hi zh vi (0 missing each)
Strings: 2 new sentences (ids t1706223d and t6a964418), already translated into es, hi, zh, vi inside this patch

